---
import '../styles/global.css';
const title = 'Privacy | Awesome Jev';
const description = 'How Awesome Jev handles analytics, messages, and external links.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://jevbest.com/privacy/" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>{title}</title>
  </head>
  <body class="policy-body">
    <main class="policy-page">
      <a class="policy-back" href="/">← Awesome Jev</a>
      <p class="section-kicker">SITE INFORMATION</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="policy-updated">Last updated September 19, 2026</p>
      <h2>What does this site collect?</h2>
      <p>Awesome Jev uses Google Analytics to understand aggregate site usage, such as page visits, device type, and referring pages. Google may set cookies or process technical identifiers according to its own policies. The catalog does not provide user accounts or sell personal information.</p>
      <h2>What happens when you contact us?</h2>
      <p>If you email the maintainer or submit a GitHub issue, the information you provide is used to respond to the message or review the submission. GitHub and your email provider process that information under their own terms.</p>
      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>The catalog links to third-party repositories and websites. Their privacy practices are outside Awesome Jev’s control, so review the destination’s policies before sharing personal information.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this notice can be sent to <a href="mailto:someuxyz@gmail.com">someuxyz@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
